{"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"title":"WordNet Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/WordNet","doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/Synset","doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/POS"],"anchor":"WordNet-Types"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP"]]},"metadata":{"title":"WordNet Semantic Hierarchy & Lexical Graphs","modules":[{"name":"SwiftNLP"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/WordNetAndLexicalGraphs"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"WordNet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a large lexical database of English where nouns, verbs, adjectives, and adverbs are organized into sets of cognitive synonyms called ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Synsets","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", interlinked by conceptual-semantic and lexical relations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"1. Looking Up Synsets & Definitions","anchor":"1-Looking-Up-Synsets--Definitions"},{"code":["import SwiftNLP","","let wordnet = WordNet.shared","","\/\/ Look up all noun synsets for \"bank\"","let synsets = wordnet.synsets(for: \"bank\", pos: .noun)","for s in synsets {","    print(\"ID: \\(s.id), Definition: \\(s.definition)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"2. Semantic Similarity Metrics","anchor":"2-Semantic-Similarity-Metrics"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftSci implements standard lexical similarity algorithms:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Path Similarity","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Shortest path distance in the hypernym taxonomy:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Formula:"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sim_path(s1, s2) = 1 \/ (1 + distance(s1, s2))"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wu-Palmer Similarity (WUP)","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Measures depth of least common subsumer (LCS) relative to synset depths:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Formula:"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sim_wup(s1, s2) = (2 · depth(LCS)) \/ (depth(s1) + depth(s2))"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}]},{"code":["let dog = wordnet.synset(\"dog.n.01\")!","let cat = wordnet.synset(\"cat.n.01\")!","","let pathSim = wordnet.pathSimilarity(dog, cat)","let wupSim = wordnet.wuPalmerSimilarity(dog, cat)","","print(\"Path Similarity: \\(pathSim), Wu-Palmer: \\(wupSim)\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Navigate semantic relationships, compute synset distances, and explore English hypernym\/hyponym trees."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftnlp\/wordnetandlexicalgraphs"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftNLP/documentation/SwiftNLP/WordNet":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftnlp\/wordnet","kind":"symbol","title":"WordNet","abstract":[{"text":"Native WordNet semantic database query engine and concept similarity computer.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/WordNet","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WordNet","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WordNet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftNLP/documentation/SwiftNLP/P